<title>GREECE: ALPHA CREDIT BANK KEEPS PRIME RATE UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>ALPHA CREDIT BANK KEEPS PRIME RATE UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Credit Bank will</p>
<p>keep its prime rate for working capital and fixed asset loans</p>
<p>unchanged at 12.50 percent, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Alpha Credit, which reviews its rates weekly, said the</p>
<p>maximum add-on would remain unchanged at 3.5 percent.</p>
<p>Its adjustable mortgage mortgages were steady at 13.0</p>
<p>percent.</p>
<p>The bank launched 15-year mortgages in October 1995 with</p>
<p>rates set at 12.0 percent for the first five years. Rates on</p>
<p>these mortgages currently stand at 10.50 percent.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
